+## Historical evidence boundary
+
+The [Core compatibility receipt](../../validation/evidence/unity-6000.3-settings-core-windows-editor/compatibility-receipt.json)
+and [Unity adapter compatibility receipt](../../validation/evidence/unity-6000.3-settings-unity-windows-editor/compatibility-receipt.json)
+each record revision `7753de2bb10eb6376bc0f1df48bfd74ee3bf1ed9`:
+Core `0.1.0` alone for the Core receipt, and Core plus Unity adapter `0.1.0`
+for the adapter receipt. Their linked compile and EditMode results passed on
+2026-07-16. The release tag is a separate installation boundary, not the recorded
+test revision.
+
+Both receipts bind the same exact host tuple: Unity / Unity Editor `6000.3.19f1`,
+`WindowsEditor`, graphics API `Null`, scripting backend `Mono`, architecture
+`x86_64`, and `windows-editor-host` version `10.0.26200`. Renderer, XR provider,
+runtime, and input routes are `not_applicable`. Requested Test Framework is
+`1.6.0`; resolved dependencies are `com.unity.test-framework` `1.6.0`,
+`com.unity.ext.nunit` `2.0.5`, `com.unity.modules.imgui` `1.0.0`, and
+`com.unity.modules.jsonserialize` `1.0.0`. Each receipt links its own manifest,
+lockfile and digests; [compatibility profiles](../../../compatibility-profiles.json)
+remain the authoritative tuple registry.
+
+These are historical compile/EditMode passes for those recorded consumers, not
+execution evidence for later source or sample changes, which remain unexecuted
+unless separately evidenced. This documentation correction does not rerun Unity
+or prove current-head support. Renderer, accessibility-outcome, and named-device
+behavior remain unverified; no other Editor, host, backend, input, provider, or
+device tuple inherits these results.
